# Changelog

## v1.1.1

Post-publication update of Elementti.

### Added

* **Area analysis (new optional step 8).** Draw one or more regions on a map or reference image (rectangle, square, ellipse, polygon, or freehand) and get the mean value of the selected maps, ratios, and formulas inside each region, for example steel, corrosion-product layer, and deposit. Regions can be edited, undone, deleted, or cleared. The map can be zoomed, panned, and fitted to the window.
  * Saves a table of region values (`area_analysis.csv`), the region outlines (`area_analysis_regions.csv`), and a two-panel figure with the regions on the map and a chart comparing them.
  * **Detail box:** zoom into part of the map and analyse only that area, with its own map, chart, and CSV outputs.
  * **Excel report** (`.xlsx`) with the results, detailed statistics, analysis settings, and figures.
  * **Copy results** button for pasting region values into other programs.
* **Quick export buttons** on the Display, Line profile, and Area analysis pages to save the current map, chart, or CSV without running Generate.
* **Group formatting** on the Display page copies chosen appearance settings from one output to other outputs.
* **Review acquisition groups** in step 1 proposes which files belong to the same acquisition, based on metadata or shared file-name prefixes. You can check and change the selection before using it.
* **Review import suggestions** in step 4 proposes rows to remove, columns to remove, and scale factors from each file's contents and metadata. Only the settings you tick are applied.
* **Source file verification.** Elementti records a SHA-256 fingerprint of every input file. **Review source files** shows files that are changed, missing, or unverified, and records an explicit decision when a changed file is accepted. The project file and the Word report include this information.
* **Save Word report** option on the Generate page. Uncheck it to skip the `.docx` report.

### Changed

* Elementti now has nine steps: Area analysis is step 8 and Generate is step 9.
* The project file format was updated to version 4. Projects saved with v1.1.0 still open.
* The Word report also includes maps, charts, area-analysis results, and source-file verification.
* The new optional dependency `openpyxl` is needed only for Excel reports and was added to `requirements.txt`.

## v1.1.0

Post-publication feature update of Elementti. The minor version number is raised because this release adds new functionality and changes which record files are saved with the outputs.

### Added

* **Projects.** Every time **Generate** is clicked, Elementti saves a project file, `Project.elementti.json`, that records every setting of every step.
* **Open project** button in step 1 that reads a saved project back with all its settings:
  * **Its own map files** makes the same outputs again. If the map files were moved, Elementti asks for the folder that contains them.
  * **Other map files** uses the same settings with new maps, for example another sample measured the same way. Files with identical names are matched automatically, and every other map is chosen in a matching dialog.
* **Detailed explanations.docx.** A Word document saved with the outputs that explains every step of the run in words, formulas, and tables, including what each rule changed. It ends with a description of the run that can be adapted for the methods section of a paper. It is written with the Python standard library only, so Microsoft Word is not needed to create it.
* **How it works** windows for preprocessing, ratio and formula maps, grayscale masking, low-value protection, conditional rules, colour scales, scale bars, and line profiles. Each one explains the method in full, with its formula and a worked example.
* **Step list** on the left of the window that shows the eight steps (Files, Names, Outputs, Preprocessing, Masking and noise, Display, Line profile, Generate). Finished steps can be clicked to go back. Page titles now read "Step N of 8".
* **Progress window** while outputs are generated, so Elementti stays responsive during long runs.
* **Create Elementti.exe** button on the welcome page, available when Elementti is run from the `.py` file. It builds a single program file that starts without Python. PyInstaller is installed automatically the first time, which needs an internet connection once. On Windows, the program is signed automatically if a code-signing certificate is installed; otherwise it is left unsigned.
* Command-line options:
  * `--make-exe [folder]` builds `Elementti.exe` from the console and prints progress.
  * `--check-demo` makes the demo outputs in a temporary folder without opening a window, as a quick installation check.
* **Copy citation** button on the final page.

### Changed

* The logo and the Windows icon are built into the source file, so the single `.py` file is all that is needed. The separate `icoElementti_*.ico` and `pngElementti_*.png` resource files are no longer required.
* The JSON summary file and the plain-text methods file are replaced by `Project.elementti.json` and `Detailed explanations.docx`, which contain the same information and more.
* Message boxes use buttons that say what they do.
* Help texts were updated to describe projects, the new record files, and the new windows.

## v1.0.9

Post-publication update of Elementti.

### Added

* Added a per-output **Tick size** control that sets the font size of the colorbar numbers.
* Added a per-output **Text size** control that sets the font size of the colorbar text label.
* Added matching **Tick size** and **Text size** controls to the line profile, covering axis numbers, axis labels, title, legend, and map-panel labels.
* Recorded the new size, label, and x-axis-label settings in the JSON summary and methods text for traceability.

### Changed

* Updated the in-app citation to the published SoftwareX reference, with the paper title shown in bold.
* Placed the citation DOI on its own line and made it a clickable link that opens in the browser.
* Tick size and Text size are typed as whole numbers from `8` to `20`, showing the real default of `10` instead of the word **Default**.
* Shortened the display-settings column headers for readability: **Bar side**, **Bar label**, **Data min**, **Data max**, **Disp min**, **Disp max**, and **Tick size**.
* Data min and Data max are now shown rounded to at most four decimals.
* Disp min and Disp max now accept at most four decimals.
* Made the Disp min/max and Tick/Text size columns more compact so **Bins** and **Bin colors** keep enough width.
* Updated icon and welcome-image resource names to `icoElementti_1_0_9.ico` and `pngElementti_1_0_9.png`. Older resource names still load as a fallback.

### Fixed

* Fixed the line-profile x-axis label: it starts filled with the automatic distance label as normal editable text, and clearing it now shows no x-axis label.

## v1.0.8

Post-publication update of Elementti.

### Changed

* Simplified demo loading to one **Load demo data** option.
* Demo data are fixed and repeatable by default.
* Demo CSV files include metadata rows and detectable pixel-size information.
* Improved demo temporary-folder handling and cleanup.
* Updated icon and welcome-image resource names to `icoElementti_1_0_8.ico` and `pngElementti_1_0_8.png`.
* Improved Windows app icon handling for EXE/taskbar use.
* Removed unused old preview code.

### Fixed

* Added safer export filenames to prevent accidental overwriting.

## v1.0.7

* Made line-length labels draw above the red arrow.
* Improved automatic guide-bar endpoint rounding, for example `1.78378` becomes `1.8`.
* Made line-profile legends draw above curves for better readability.

## v1.0.6

* Reduced guide-bar and y-axis label clutter near clipped endpoint labels.
* Added line-profile legend placement option: **Inside plot** or **Outside right**.

## v1.0.5

* Added clearer display min/max guide-bar labels such as `≥21` and `≤0`.
* Line-profile x-axis now uses physical distance when pixel size is available.
* Added dual y-axes for mixed element and ratio profiles.
* Added optional manual y-axis limits for line profiles.

## v1.0.4

* Simplified the formula-map interface.
* Moved formula examples into **Read instructions**.
* Changed line-profile end marker to an arrow to show direction.

## v1.0.3

* Added custom formula maps.
* Supports expressions such as `X + Y / Z`, `(X + Y) / Z`, `X / (Y + Z)`, `sqrt(X)`, and `log10(X)`.
* Input names with spaces or symbols can be written as `[Exact input name]` or `{Exact input name}`.
* Added safe formula parsing and validation.

## v1.0.2

* Added unit-aware pixel-size handling.
* Pixel size can be detected or entered in `nm`, `um/µm`, `mm`, `cm`, or `m`.
* Values are converted internally to `µm/pixel`.

## v1.0.1

* Added dynamic display.
* Added linescan.

## v1.0.0

* Original baseline version.

## Notes

* The SoftwareX-published baseline version is **v1.0.0**.
* The current updated post-publication version is **v1.1.1**.
* Latest version file: `src/elementti.py`.
* Always check detected pixel size before final export.
* Display min/max changes the color scale; it does not remove data.
* Values above display max use the top color, and values below display min use the bottom color.
